id: pm-jev-79ht
title: Explain incompatible joint decision proposals before apply
description: Validate selected typed answers against caller-declared cross-question constraints and host relationship rules without changing model answers or tracker state.
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[2]: constraints,joint-decisions
created_at: "2026-10-28T20:38:13.829Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-28T22:39:40.592Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: "A mutually exclusive classification pair produces a two-answer witness; validator never silently edits model answers; a failed constraint produces zero mutations; typed SDK and CLI with compact TOON/JSON, typed refusals and remedies; documented example and measured public tracker validation."
comments[15]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-28T20:38:33.857Z",codex-agent,"Overlap recheck: index.ts parseQuestionsDocument/validateAnswers validate individual typed shapes; triage/link apply individual proposals. Installed host SDK graph exports RelationshipGraph, assertHierarchyMutationAllowed, assertNonHierarchyCardinalityMutationAllowed, validateRelationshipEvents and ordering analysis; core owns mutation validation/transactions. Sibling pm-context next-evidence/witnesses select evidence, pm-review scopes validate review obligations, pm-rl handles evaluation/training; none implements caller-declared cross-question answer constraints. Plan: bounded read-only joint validation with exact choice/score/noul predicates, mutually exclusive/implication rules, compact answer witnesses and host graph checks for conditional relationship additions. No new apply, import/export/sync, journal, lease, checkpoint or status classification path; no model calls or tracker writes. Acceptance and shared safety constraints recorded before implementation."
  "2026-10-28T20:46:58.603Z",codex-agent,"Implementation: exported joint schema, validator and compact typed reports; jev validate delegates to the same SDK path. Selected choice/score values are preserved even when distributions disagree; noul predicates require exact inclusive cutoffs. Relationship additions are checked as one prospective graph via SDK edge, hierarchy, cardinality and ordering primitives. The new path is read-only and has no persistent package state. Focused tests currently pass 7/7, including 500 seeded sequences / 4000 operations, native no-Git JSON/TOON and SDK read-back preservation. Shipped SDK producer optional fields are accepted; malformed inputs are refused before client acquisition. Additional branch coverage and installation/public-copy acceptance are running."
  "2026-10-28T20:50:13.832Z",codex-agent,"Public-copy acceptance passed on unbraind/pm-lint committed public tracker: 23 SDK-read items, 52 authoritative files verified, 23 controlled incompatible batches with two-answer witnesses, 23 corrected compatible batches, 14 existing-relationship batches, 23 answer batches unchanged; exact SDK read-back and authoritative bytes unchanged, zero mutations and zero inference calls, Git unavailable during validation. Aggregate provenance and limitations are in docs/joint-decisions-evidence.json. Targeted measurement of the three new modules reached 100% statements/branches/functions/lines; whole-package release evidence remains delegated to CI at final head."
  "2026-10-28T20:53:40.027Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof ran in a disposable copy: replacing validateJointDecisions with an always-compatible result fails the exclusive-witness regression; replacing graphConflict with a no-conflict result fails the host batch-graph regression. The package worktree was never modified by either revert. Shared integrity APIs require the verified SDK 2026.10.25 surface, so the declared peer/manifest host floor is now 2026.10.25; the pinned devDependency is unchanged. Global/local package acceptance is being repeated with selected relationship cycles to force host SDK acquisition through every installation mode."
  "2026-10-28T20:56:30.387Z",codex-agent,"Current-host overlap check also inspected the installed pm-cli 2026.10.28 public SDK and sibling source surfaces. Core tool-schema cross-field rules describe pm action option combinations, not selected inference answers or cross-question semantic witnesses. Other matches were CLI flag exclusivity and training statistics. No duplicate joint-answer validator was found. Strict health passes with isolated HOME and disabled global/system Git configuration; the ordinary-shell warning is the pre-existing ambient global pm-github skew tracked by pm-jev-v2la, with no project extension or dependency-pin change required."
  "2026-10-28T20:58:24.724Z",codex-agent,"Final focused checks: 8/8 regressions pass, including the expanded 500-sequence/4000-operation model with old-input replay, CRLF variants, native parent/blocker/dependency fields, generated relationship proposals, six custom status remaps and changing ambient focus. Native SDK state is read back after every sequence. The three new modules measure 100% statements, branches, functions and lines. Compatibility floor tests pass 4/4. Typecheck, test typecheck, lint, docstrings and duplication pass (zero clones). The linked command was executed via pm test --run --progress and passed; test result tracking is disabled by existing project policy, so results are recorded here without changing that policy. Final SDK traversal also rejects shared-reference payloads before serialization can expand them."
  "2026-10-28T20:59:36.478Z",codex-agent,"Final packed acceptance passed: one archive verified by digest and required shipped files; project-local, npm global, Bun global, npx and bunx each passed incompatible classifications, compatible classifications and a selected relationship cycle through the host SDK (15 native CLI cases), plus the packed SDK import/validator case. Archive SHA-512: 2977814b4e005141bbae8bd76685cd029472fa30ef2ab57737bca67b63588bd813c4a51026b6b5688ba526f684dce8b1556a9fbe28f1b6a513dfcc23d1d6055f. No credentials were forwarded to installer children. No outstanding SDK capability gap; existing ambient global extension skew remains separately tracked by pm-jev-v2la. The full npm and Bun release gates will run in CI at the committed PR head; no local full-suite load was added. This item stays in progress for orchestrator verification and closure."
  "2026-10-28T21:12:12.708Z",codex-agent,"CI run https://github.com/unbraind/pm-jev/actions/runs/40768368023 at 94b6dc6 passed 385/385 tests with zero skips on Node 22, but the native Node coverage gate found 99.85% function coverage: the callback inspecting existing ordering components had no pre-existing-cycle fixture. The separate c8 report was 100% and did not reveal this missing native coverage. Added a real-SDK regression that seeds an ordering cycle, checks an unchanged edge plus an unrelated addition, and reads current native state back unchanged. This also extends the legacy-data allow corpus. No production implementation or thresholds changed; final-head npm/Bun evidence will come from a fresh CI run."
  "2026-10-28T21:16:55.578Z",codex-agent,"The expanded legacy-cycle allow regression now passes under native Node coverage: 8/8 targeted tests, zero skips, 100% lines/branches/functions across joint-command.ts, joint-decisions.ts and joint-schema.ts. Exact command: node --test --test-concurrency=2 --experimental-test-coverage --test-coverage-include=joint-decisions.ts --test-coverage-include=joint-schema.ts --test-coverage-include=joint-command.ts --test-coverage-lines=100 --test-coverage-branches=100 --test-coverage-functions=100 test/joint-decisions.test.ts. Build/test typecheck, lint, docstrings and duplication also pass. Initial Node 26 CI confirmed the same coverage-only gap with 385/385 tests passing and zero skips; the new test closes it without production changes or threshold changes. All tracker writes are finishing before the next exact-head CI run."
  "2026-10-28T21:18:01.188Z",codex-agent,"Final artifact acceptance will be repeated after the test-only follow-up commit, so its one captured archive also includes the generated changelog at the final head. The final archive digest and exact-head CI gate counts will be recorded on the PR without moving the head again. The prior archive acceptance receipt remains valid for those exact earlier bytes."
  "2026-10-28T22:06:02.805Z",codex-agent,"Resumed for PR 65 auto re-review round 1. Worktree is clean; origin/main is fully contained in this branch (two commits ahead, zero behind), so no merge is needed. General rule: propagate the same caller/workspace relationship registry through construction, integrity checks and every derived graph analysis; never reconstruct custom semantics with a built-in default. Whole-package audit found both before/after analyzeRelationshipExecution calls in joint-decisions.ts omit the registry; edge/hierarchy/cardinality checks already pass it. Auditing other commands, SDK/CLI, serializers, tests and packed consumers for the same class; the supplied review names one blocking finding, and additional posted findings are being checked. Existing completed feature work and evidence are retained."
  "2026-10-28T22:16:12.804Z",codex-agent,"Class-wide regressions reproduced both omissions independently before the fix: new custom proposals threw in after-graph analysis, and real SDK-persisted custom edges threw in before-graph analysis. The 500-case custom-registry property passes after forwarding {registry} to both calls. Native JSON/TOON testing also exposed a bundled-context issue: the focused graph SDK resolver does not see host-contributed registrations in the CLI. All workspace registry resolution in index.ts, tracker-evaluation.ts and joint-decisions.ts now uses the aggregate public SDK seam, with graph primitives still receiving explicit registries. No further actionable findings were present in PR reviews or inline comments; quota/skip notices are missing review evidence, not approvals. The coverage runner is capped at two workers for the requested full gates; no thresholds or tests are removed."
  "2026-10-28T22:25:47.672Z",codex-agent,"Revert proof completed in a disposable copy with a passing fixed architecture baseline before/after: independently removing the before-graph registry, removing the after-graph registry, or restoring focused-registry acquisition in joint-decisions.ts, index.ts or tracker-evaluation.ts makes the targeted regression fail for its intended reason. Removing the two-worker cap fails the existing gate-runner contract test. All six mutants failed, no package-worktree mutation was used, and assertions checked the expected failure reason. New runtime regressions passed together with the coverage-gate tests (26/26); the package-wide AST contract additionally passed and covers every production root/script consumer. Host TOON legitimately omits empty collections; tests compare semantic receipts while retaining exact JSON equality. Packed acceptance now covers custom stored edges/aliases/order/association in JSON and TOON in all five invocation modes plus Node/Bun SDK overrides."
  "2026-10-28T22:31:11.043Z",codex-agent,"Linked registry regression executed successfully with pm test --run --progress --match joint-registry: 3/3, zero test skips; existing project policy disables automatic result tracking, so results are recorded here. This covers every production consumer, 500 registry permutations, persisted custom edges, both directions, aliases, association and native JSON/TOON. The entire package scan found exactly two missing analysis options and three focused registry imports; all five are fixed and independently guarded. No additional actionable non-blocking findings were supplied or posted. Full npm/Bun release gates will run in CI with the committed two-worker cap, consistent with the original saturated-host instruction; thresholds remain unchanged."
  "2026-10-28T22:39:34.564Z",codex-agent,"Expanded packed acceptance passed 1/1 using one archive: 45 native CLI cases across project-local, npm global, Bun global, npx and bunx, including stored custom kinds in JSON/TOON; seven packed SDK cases include Node and Bun registry overrides. Archive SHA-512: 44b212c8b9b067d740a975f947d57d9ff74c2577e1aef5b5bbac01843087863dee744690ad7a074582805bd3dd47ea5aca527aeebcf67ee7ff91cdb7680547ce. Public-copy revalidation remains 23 items, 52 authoritative files, 23 incompatible plus 23 compatible controls and 14 existing edges, exact SDK/file read-back unchanged, zero mutations/inference. Typecheck, test typecheck, lint, docstrings, provenance and zero-duplication checks pass. All provided review findings and the additional registry-context class instances are addressed; fresh exact-head CI gate counts and the artifact identity verification will be recorded on PR 65 without further tracker writes."
